{{!-- SITES — interesting places the PCs can explore. A SECTION at the foot of the Expeditions
      tab, having been a tab of its own here and, before that, a tab on the steading sheet.

      WHY IT SITS UNDER EXPEDITIONS. Its own first sentence already said so: a site is "the
      destination of an expedition, a point of interest on the way, or an incidental discovery."
      What a GM writes up here is what a trip is FOR, and keeping the two a rail-click apart meant
      the sites for tonight's journey could never be seen beside the journey.

      IT FOLDS, AND STARTS OPEN, like every other section on this sheet and for the same reason: a
      section shut on first open is one a GM never learns is there. It is the longest thing on the
      panel when a world has a dozen sites written up — a site is a page-long card — and that is
      what the caret is for: folding it is one click and is then remembered per user, which is the
      right way round, since a GM three sessions in can choose that for themselves and a GM one
      session in must not have it chosen for them.

      NO `startCollapsed`, therefore. That parameter is for sections that are reference rather than
      content (the toolkit's prep guidance), and its absence is what makes a stored id here mean
      "this GM folded it" — see section-collapse.hbs for how the two readings are told apart.

      THE BOX AROUND THE PAIR IS LOAD-BEARING. A fold hides its heading's FOLLOWING SIBLINGS
      (`_sectionFoldTargets`), so without this wrapper the walk would run on past the section and
      out of the tab. Nothing else may go in this box, and a SECOND heading in it would stop the
      caret claiming at the first — the same rule the Completed fold above it keeps.

      NOT INSIDE `.stonetop-gm-encounters`, the section holding the expedition cards, but a
      sibling of it. That section is the one the tab's pencil locks (`--reading`) and the one
      whose flex column spaces the cards; sites are gated by neither, and this tab having one
      pencil that reaches exactly two delete buttons is a property worth not blurring.

      THE STORAGE DID NOT MOVE and must not. A site is a JournalEntryPage inside a hidden
      per-steading JournalEntry, pointed at by a flag on the STEADING actor — see the header of
      module/actors/gmtoolkit/gm-prep-tabs.js, which spells out the silent data-loss path.

      NO SECTION PENCIL, unlike the Threats tab, and so no `stonetop-readonly` either. A pencil
      gates the fields you type into, and this section has none: a site is written up in the
      wizard and re-opened in it, its d20 tables roll without writing anything, and the only
      control left is the trash. Gating that ONE button behind a pencil bought nothing and cost
      the obvious reading of the toolbar — the trash sat beside a live pencil and was simply
      mouse-dead, when the confirm dialog it already opens is the real "are you sure".

      The `steading-*` class names are CSS hooks kept deliberately; they and the storage rule are
      explained at length in gm-toolkit-tab-threats.hbs and in gm-prep-tabs.js. Every listener
      this section needs is scoped to `.steading-sites` rather than to a panel, which is why the
      move cost the mixin nothing. --}}
<div class="stonetop-gm-expedition-sites">
	{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.sites")
	    note=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.sitesNote")
	    collapse="gm-expeditions-sites"}}
	<section class="sheet-tab steading-sites steading-prep-cards">

		{{#if stonetop.hasSteading}}
		<p class="steading-threats-intro">
			Interesting places the PCs can explore (Book I, <em>Sites</em>): the destination of an expedition, a point of interest on the way, or an incidental discovery. Written up here for your eyes only. Drag a card onto a scene to pin it to the map.
		</p>

		{{#if stonetop.sites.length}}
		<div class="steading-threats-grid">
			{{#each stonetop.sites}}
			<div class="threat-card-wrap" data-page-uuid="{{uuid}}">
				{{> "stonetop.site-card" this}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-card-tools" kind="site" uuid=uuid}}
			</div>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-add-bar" kind="site" label="Create a site"}}
		{{else}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-no-steading" noun="Sites"}}
		{{/if}}

	</section>
</div>
